From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] netprofm: network names, profiles, connectivity, costs, events and IDispatch

The Network List Manager answered much with E_NOTIMPL or a FIXME and fixed
values, and never told anyone of a change. As documented now:

- Networks: a name and description (the profile's, else the DNS suffix or
  the adapter's name), SetName and SetDescription, the category from the
  profile (public, or domain-authenticated on the machine's own domain)
  and SetCategory (public or private; E_INVALIDARG else), the times
  created and connected, and the domain type. Profiles are kept where
  Windows keeps them, HKLM\Software\Microsoft\Windows NT\CurrentVersion\
  NetworkList\Profiles\{id}, so a new manager reads them back.
- Connectivity per network, connection and machine, IPv4 and IPv6 apart:
  an address is the local network, a default route the internet (it was
  IPv4 only, from any gateway).
- Costs: from DefaultMediaCost by medium (Ethernet, WiFi, 4G, Default:
  1 unrestricted, 2 fixed), for a connection, for the machine, and for a
  destination (the connection that reaches it); SetDestinationAddresses
  is accepted.
- Events: the manager follows the host's interface, address and route
  changes (NotifyIpInterfaceChange and kin) and tells its sinks:
  INetworkListManagerEvents::ConnectivityChanged,
  INetworkEvents::NetworkConnectivityChanged,
  INetworkConnectionEvents::NetworkConnectionConnectivityChanged and
  INetworkCostManagerEvents::CostChanged. Sinks are reached through the
  global interface table, in their own apartments. EnumConnections and
  EnumConnectionPoints are implemented; an unknown event interface is
  CONNECT_E_NOCONNECTION.
- IDispatch: a type library (netprofm_tlb.idl, NETWORKLIST) and
  GetTypeInfoCount, GetTypeInfo, GetIDsOfNames and Invoke on the manager,
  networks, connections and their enumerators, so scripts call them by
  name; _NewEnum gives an IEnumVARIANT. netlistmgr.idl gives
  INetworkListManager's methods their DISPIDs, and IsConnected and
  IsConnectedToInternet are properties (get_IsConnected, as in the SDK).

Wine's netprofm test's 4 todos pass.

Gate: test/netlist-gate.sh (in a user and network namespace with a dummy
interface; the gate adds a default route; test/netlist-probe.c). Mutants
SG_MUTANT_NO_DISPATCH, SG_MUTANT_NO_EVENTS, SG_MUTANT_NO_MEDIA_COST
(netprofm/list.c).
